    "claim": "The workbench command code pane edits the SIGNATURE, not just the body: a params input + return-type select (.wcc-sig-row, patch mode only; the read-only .wcc-sig span otherwise). Signature edits join the dirty check, and the save routes through upsert_command - the only command that writes returntype/params - carrying the current body and imports in that one call (which recompiles). Trade-off: unlike patch_command_body's exact-match guard, that path is unguarded - the editor's copy wins.",
    "detail": "dev.workbench patches p91-p98 (2026-08-14). An off-list returntype (e.g. InputStream) is kept as its own select option: shown faithfully, and a save keeping it fails visibly at upsert_command's validation rather than being coerced. Verified end-to-end on a disposable instance with Playwright: create, retype String->JSONObject + add param, save green after matching the body, reopen shows persisted signature, body-only edits still travel the patch_command_body path.",
